nt><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI, MASASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOINUMA, HIDEOMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI MASASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOINUMA HIDEOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI, MASASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOINUMA, HIDEOMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A laser device (20) is used to form thin film on a substrate (1) in a film forming process, and irradiates the substrate (1) placed in a vacuum chamber (101) of a film-forming device (100) to heat it to a predetermined temperature. A laser beam is led in the vicinity of the substrate (1) through an optical fiber (23) and irradiates the substrate (1) directly or indirectly at the end of the optical fiber (23). The optical fiber (23) is held in a vacuum pipe (24), and the laser beam passing through the end of the optical fiber (23) is reflected to the substrate (1) by a reflector (33). The use of a laser beam allows an insulating substrate to be heated in an oxidative atmosphere.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce dispositif à laser (20), utilisé pour former une couche mince sur un substrat lors d'un processus de mise au point de film, soumet à un rayonnement le substrat (1) placé dans la chambre à vide (101) d'un dispositif de formation de film (100) et ce, pour amener ce substrat à une température prédéterminée. Le faisceau laser, qui est amené au voisinage du substrat (1) par une fibre optique (23), le soumet à un rayonnement direct ou indirect au sortir de la fibre optique (23). La fibre optique (23) se trouve dans un conduit sous vide (24) et le faisceau laser passant par l'extrémité de celle-ci (23) est réfléchi vers le substrat (1) par un réflecteur (33). L'utilisation d'un faisceau laser permet de chauffer un substrat isolant dans une atmosphère oxydante.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>